==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16~30 seconds<sup>480f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16~30 seconds<sup>480f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16~30 seconds<sup>480f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Othom]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 16~40 seconds<sup>480f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Loris|Lorises]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage features a deadly combination of Sir Rel and Celeboodle to kill short-ranged Cats, Othom and Mooth to serve as walls, and Lorises to kill backliners. Thankfully the Sir Rels are limited, so defeating all of them will create an opening to begin killing the other enemies. Short-ranged but fast units will work well for this stage, since they can dodge the Lorises and land hits on peons or Sir Rels easily.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]]: Both are fast meatshields that can easily sneak into the blind spot of the Lorises to tank hits.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk]]/[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: Brainwashed Mohawk and Maize serve similar purposes to Manic Mohawk and Manic Eraser respectively, but both likely won't be available on {{1c}} due to the difficulty of their unlock stages. When they are unlocked, though, they're very powerful for this stage.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Slime Cat has short range and fast speed, plus can clear out the annoying peons like Doge and Snache for other units. They can also take huge chunks out of the Sir Rel and Celeboodle's health.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman deals massive damage to the Mooths and Othom, which makes them a very useful rusher for this stage.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: Maglev is another unit useful for rushing in and getting a hit off. They also earn double money if they land the last hit on an enemy, making them extra useful for earning money.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]: While Slapstick Cats aren't particularly fast, their high health vs. Relics lets these lovebirds waltz up to the frontline and land hits with ease. Their Weaken Talent can also help a lot, if it is unlocked.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: Doron definitely won't be available on {{1c}} due to only being unlocked later on in Uncanny Legends, but in {{2c}} and beyond he's very useful here, since the Sir Rels can't shred his staggeringly high health. His Freezing Surge will also sync the attacks of the Lorises (assuming it hits them both), which provides slower units such as [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] a chance to land hits.

